1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,410
Ten miles from the ocean.
Never touched the sand.

2
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:00,820
Mom worked three jobs.
She never complained.

3
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:01,229
We didn't go to the beach.
The beach wasn't for us.

4
00:00:01,229 --> 00:00:01,639
My father died when I was seven.

5
00:00:01,639 --> 00:00:02,049
Shot in a ditch
with seventeen dollars.

6
00:00:02,049 --> 00:00:02,459
He loved us.
He loved the street more.

7
00:00:02,459 --> 00:00:02,870
Got arrested as a kid.
Stupid stuff.

8
00:00:02,870 --> 00:00:03,279
Then at twenty-one,
I was framed.

9
00:00:03,279 --> 00:00:03,690
Learned to code
on a broken computer.

10
00:00:03,690 --> 00:00:04,099
Interview goes great.
Then: background check.

11
00:00:04,099 --> 00:00:04,509
Door after door
slams shut.

12
00:00:04,509 --> 00:00:04,919
I'm drowning.

13
00:00:04,919 --> 00:00:05,330
I built an app.
Called it No Sand Beach.

14
00:00:05,330 --> 00:00:05,740
Rewrote my background.
Gave myself a fake degree.

15
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:06,150
Got the job.
Got the office.
Got the view.

16
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:06,559
I forgot my mother's laugh.
I forgot my brother's voice.

17
00:00:06,559 --> 00:00:06,969
I was becoming
a stranger to myself.

18
00:00:06,969 --> 00:00:07,379
Dad appeared as a glitch:
"You're killing her by becoming someone else."

19
00:00:07,379 --> 00:00:07,790
I collapsed on the office floor.
Mom held my hand.
Marcus came.
We reconciled.

20
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:08,199
I deleted it. Line by line.
Got my real memories back.

21
00:00:08,199 --> 00:00:08,609
Touched the sand.

Love isn't a subscription.
It's the ground under your feet.

You don't have to erase who you are.

